WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:06.068
<v Examiner>Name the four groups of risk factors for substance abuse in young adults,

2
00:00:06.068 --> 00:00:07.791
<v Examiner>and give an example of one.

3
00:00:07.791 --> 00:00:08.429
<v Examiner>Two marks.

4
00:00:08.879 --> 00:00:10.443
The hook: F, I, S, B.

5
00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.423
Family, individual, social, behavioural.

6
00:00:13.873 --> 00:00:17.108
This slide has no Pusheen, so learn all four.

7
00:00:17.108 --> 00:00:18.187
Family-related.

8
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:18.978
Individual.

9
00:00:18.978 --> 00:00:20.775
Social and environmental.

10
00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:21.638
Behavioural.

11
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.868
Examples, from the brainstorm in her notes.

12
00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:29.006
Family: relatives who use, stress in the home, childhood trauma.

13
00:00:29.006 --> 00:00:33.338
Individual: an impulsive personality, mental ill health, or access,

14
00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:36.183
like an injury that leads to a prescription.

15
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:41.873
Social and environmental: peer influence, cultural and societal acceptance, and the law.

16
00:00:41.873 --> 00:00:45.171
Behavioural: frequent use, often starting socially.

17
00:00:46.621 --> 00:00:47.787
Who takes drugs?

18
00:00:47.787 --> 00:00:49.463
Her answer: anyone can.

19
00:00:49.463 --> 00:00:52.451
Across gender, age, ethnicity and income.

20
00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:53.835
Avoid stereotyping.

21
00:00:53.835 --> 00:00:57.479
And all drugs, medicines included, can be misused.

22
00:00:57.929 --> 00:00:59.552
The picture in Aotearoa.

23
00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:03.607
These slides all have Pusheen, so no statistic is for marks.

24
00:01:03.607 --> 00:01:09.149
The concept: most adults drink alcohol, and a real share drink in a hazardous way.

25
00:01:09.149 --> 00:01:13.813
Daily vaping is now more common than smoking, and among young people,

26
00:01:13.813 --> 00:01:16.855
smoking is more common in lower income areas,

27
00:01:16.855 --> 00:01:20.234
while vaping is more common in higher income ones.

28
00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:26.318
Cannabis is the most used illicit drug, and MDMA, cocaine and opioid use have been rising.

29
00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:31.252
The numbers come from the New Zealand Health Survey, the Drug Foundation,

30
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:34.631
wastewater testing, and the Youth Nineteen survey.

31
00:01:35.081 --> 00:01:35.655
<v Examiner>Once more.

32
00:01:35.655 --> 00:01:37.492
<v Examiner>The four groups of risk factors.

33
00:01:39.942 --> 00:01:45.198
Four groups of risk factors for substance abuse in young adults: family-related,

34
00:01:45.198 --> 00:01:48.812
like relatives who use or childhood trauma; individual,

35
00:01:48.812 --> 00:01:53.871
like an impulsive personality or mental ill health; social and environmental,

36
00:01:53.871 --> 00:01:57.879
like peer influence and societal acceptance; and behavioural,

37
00:01:57.879 --> 00:02:00.507
like frequent use that started socially.

38
00:02:00.507 --> 00:02:03.332
Anyone can take drugs, so don't stereotype.
